physical therapy** with progressive balance and strength training (e.g., tai chi), (3) **Occupational therapy** for home safety modifications and adaptive strategies, (4) Treatment of underlying conditions (e.g., orthostatic hypotension, vision impairment). Benzodiazepines are **contraindicated** (Beers Criteria) as they increase fall risk. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 12; Current Geriatrics; JAGS 2011)'),
